# Payment methods

A payment method is the identifier where the money was sent: a card, a Mexican CLABE, a bank account number, or a crypto wallet. Callers send `reference` only. `type` is prohibited on `StorePaymentMethodRequest`, `PaymentMethodRequest`, and on report payment-method objects. `PaymentMethodType::fromReference` chooses the type. The matching value object then accepts or rejects the value.

`reference` is a required string, max 255, trimmed before the rules run.

## How the type is chosen

`App\Domain\PaymentMethod\Enums\PaymentMethodType`:

| Case | Value | When |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `CARD_NUMBER` | 1 | 16 digits after non-digits are removed |
| `CLABE` | 2 | 18 digits after non-digits are removed |
| `ACCOUNT_NUMBER` | 3 | 10 digits after non-digits are removed |
| `WALLET` | 4 | the trimmed reference matches a wallet pattern below, checked before digit length |
| `OTHER` | 5 | anything else, including an empty string |

Wallet patterns, in `PaymentMethodType::isCryptoWallet`:

- Ethereum: `0x` plus 40 hex digits.
- Legacy Bitcoin: `1` or `3`, then 25–34 base58 characters.
- Bech32 Bitcoin: `bc1` or `tb1`, then 25–87 alphanumeric characters.
- Tron: `T` plus 33 base58 characters.

## What is stored

Value objects live in `App\Domain\PaymentMethod\ValueObjects`. Non-digits are stripped before the length check for card, CLABE, and account. The stored value is digits only.

- `CardNumber`: exactly 16 digits. Reject with `Card number must be 16 digits long.` Example input `4152 3412 5132 1531`.
- `Clabe`: exactly 18 digits. Reject with `CLABE must be 18 digits long.` Example input `032 180 000118359719`.
- `AccountNumber`: exactly 10 digits. Reject with `Account number must be exactly 10 digits long.` Example input `010 3215312`.
- `Reference` (wallet and other): remove spaces, then store the rest. Example wallet `1A1zP1eP5QGefi2DMPTfTL5SLmv7DivfNa`.

Persist with `PaymentMethodRepository::firstOrCreate`. Attach the row through the scammer or organization repository. Do not set `type` from the request body.
